    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1866-a1">

                <pb facs="1377" n="1261" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1261"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary for Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. S–7377.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to advise you of
                    the receipt of the polite note of your excellency, No. 186, of June 10 last,
                    relating to the late William T. Harrington.</p>
                <p>The note referred to has been sent to the Consulting Attorney of this office for
                    his study and consideration, and as soon as his opinion is received it will be a
                    pleasure to forward his reply to your excellency concerning this particular.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. T. Lefevre.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
